# This module's Go sources are LF in the index and must be LF in the worktree
# too. gofmt compares the bytes ON DISK, so a CRLF checkout makes `gofmt -l`
# list a file that is byte-identical to a clean one — measured: main.go's entire
# gofmt diff was 578 lines of ^M and nothing else. eol=lf overrides
# core.autocrlf=true, which is what put the CRLF there in the first place.
*.go text eol=lf

# Nothing under bin/ is committed any more: the image builds the CLI from a
# pinned upstream commit (see the Dockerfile). This rule stays as a guard: if a
# binary is ever added under bin/ again, git must never convert its bytes.
# `binary` is the -text -diff -merge macro.
bin/** binary

# History note: the vendored linux CLI binary used to be tracked with Git LFS
# here (40 distinct blobs, the packed repository at 127 MiB, measured on
# 2026-09-20). The binary and vendor-cli.sh were removed together with that
# rule. The old blobs and their LFS objects stay in the history: removing them
# means rewriting history, which invalidates every existing clone and every
# commit hash. That is a separate decision.